    <string name="familie_presence_title">Who is home</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_share">Share presence</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_share_desc">The app tells your family\'s server only „home“ or „away“, recognised by the home network – no GPS. You can switch it off any time.</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_consent_title">Share presence?</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_consent_text">When your phone is in the home network (the server\'s own network or the network behind one of its gateways), the app reports „home“, otherwise „away“ – also in the background, at most every two minutes. To check, the app sends your phone\'s local network address (e.g. 192.168.1.23) to your server; no location, no Wi-Fi name. Your family sees it in the app, on the wall tablet and in the portal; parents can let smart-home rules react to it (e.g. heating down when everyone is away). It is stored only on your family\'s GateControl server. You can switch it off at any time.</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_consent_yes">Share</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_now_home">This phone is home now.</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_now_away">This phone is away now.</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_now_unknown">Checking the network …</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_now_undecided">Can\'t tell right now – the last state stays.</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_old_server">Your GateControl server is older than 1.167: it recognises home only when it is itself in your home network, and only while the VPN is connected. From 1.167 on, a gateway in the home network is enough, with or without VPN.</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_unsupported">Your GateControl server cannot check the home network yet – please update it.</string>
    <string name="familie_presence_check_failed">The server can\'t be reached right now – the app keeps the last state and checks again later.</string>
